# `M197` (tflw D1024) — `C97`'s override leg. The default base points at a port nothing listens on
# (`:1`), so a run that reaches the arrival server at all did so through `TFLW_C97_BASE`; and a run
# with the variable unset must fail against `:1`, which is what proves the literal is the default
# and not decoration. `second` stays a plain literal beside it — the two forms mix on one env.
env local default
  api env TFLW_C97_BASE default "http://127.0.0.1:1/base"
  api second "http://127.0.0.1:4507/second"
